   "widgets_values": [
    "Krea 2 Concept Slider V1 - full showcase\n\nSix user-made sliders on one prompt, plus a same-seed comparison branch.\nQueue once, look at three things: the WITH image, the WITHOUT image, and\nthe slider report (top).\n\nThe sliders:\n1 - brightness +3 (auto poles): the reliable working band.\n2 - fog density +2 (auto): subtle atmosphere. Multi-word descriptions work.\n3 - height -4 (custom poles): a negative direction done right - the decrease\n    pole names concrete stature (\"a very short man with a small compact\n    stature, much shorter than average\"). Vague poles make weak negatives,\n    and raising push does NOT fix wording (render-proven).\n4 - age 0 (auto): parked at 0 - costs zero encoder passes; the report logs\n    the skip. Drag it to taste.\n5 - realism 0 (custom poles): a style axis - drag to -6 for a flat cartoon,\n    +6 for extra photoreal. Custom poles can be two LOOKS, not just amounts.\n6 - color saturation 0 (auto): parked.\n\nThe dial: 0 = exactly your prompt. +/-1..2 subtle, +/-3..4 working band,\n+/-5..6 maximum push (expect reframing and identity drift on people).\n\nTuning ritual:\n1. Queue once. The stack studies each active slider (1 + 2 passes per\n   active slider); parked sliders are free.\n2. Read the slider report: every slider's exact pole sentences, its push,\n   and every skip with a reason.\n3. Drag one Slider value and queue again - with \"reuse between runs\" the\n   report shows 0 new encoder passes: value drags are compose-only.\n\nThe comparison branch: WITHOUT runs the same prompt and seed through a\nslider stack with zero cards. Set every slider to 0 and the two images\ncome out identical - that is the no-change guarantee, and it also means\nthe stack is a drop-in replacement for CLIP Text Encode.\n\nLearn more: docs/concept-slider-v1.md - the full guide with the\nten-slider render audit, the slider-writing cookbook, and the worked\nweak-slider fixes."
   ],
   "title": "READ ME - showcase walkthrough"
  },
